# Machine limits (owner 2026-11-09)

The owner's machine does not cope with several copies of the app or with builds. Two rules, for every agent:

## One copy, always running, on port 3000 (owner 2026-11-09)

- The app runs on the owner's machine as **one** copy, on **port 3000**: `.claude/launch.json` → `smilesim`, which runs
  `npm run dev:local` (`scripts/dev-local.sh`): postgres and redis in their containers (no image build), the API
  compiled with `tsc --watch` and restarted on change (port 3001) with its worker, and the web in `next dev` on 3000.
- Keep it running. Every change is checked on it in the browser (`http://admin.localhost:3000`) before it is called
  done — a change is not verified by CI alone.
- Before starting it, look (`lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN`, `docker compose ps`): if it is already running and current,
  use it; if it is an older copy (another port, the Docker web/api containers, a stale build), stop that and start
  this one. Never a second web server on another port, never a second API.

## Builds run on GitHub Actions, not here

- No `npm run build`, no `docker compose up --build` / `docker build`, no Playwright e2e run (it starts its own
  servers), no full `npm run test:api` on the owner's machine or on the server. The running copy's `tsc --watch`
  and `next dev` are not builds in this sense: they recompile only what changed.
- Light checks are fine locally: `npm run lint`, `npm run check:copy`, `npm run typecheck`, and one spec file at a
  time with jest when needed.
- To build and test: push to a **work branch** (not `main`) and let `.github/workflows/ci.yml` run there. Watch the
  run (`gh run watch <id>`). When it is green, merge to `main` / push it — or tell the owner it is ready and push on
  their word. A red run is fixed on the branch first.
